<BaseLayout title="SIGWAY primordial-spectrum lab" description="Paint a primordial curvature spectrum and calculate its scalar-induced gravitational-wave response with precomputed SIGWAY kernels."><header class="page-head"><div class="shell"><span class="eyebrow">Interactive lab · SIGWAY</span><h1>From primordial structure to gravitational waves</h1><p>Choose a template or paint your own binned primordial curvature spectrum. The browser contracts it with SIGWAY’s precomputed response kernel.</p></div></header><section class="lab-stage"><div class="shell"><SigwayExplorer/></div></section><div class="prose lab-notes"><h2>What is being calculated?</h2><p>For a binned curvature spectrum, the induced signal is a bilinear contraction of bin amplitudes with a precomputed kernel. This makes genuine interactive exploration possible without running inflationary dynamics or inference in your browser.</p><p>The presets are examples, not fitted spectra. The 100-bin mode loads on demand and computes in a separate browser worker.</p></div></BaseLayout>
<style is:global>.lab-stage{background:var(--night);margin-top:clamp(2.5rem,5vw,4rem);padding-block:clamp(2rem,4vw,3.5rem)}.lab-notes{margin-top:clamp(4rem,7vw,6rem)}</style>
